 of  potential ways to go um  and any of your wisdom pearls of wisdom  would be much appreciated so whenever  someone's ready feel free to jump on and  get us kicked off  i need to go first on this one uh so  let's say for me  make it a habit to reflect sit down  reflect  journal as much as you can because it's  a practice that not only helped me as i  was applying to the gsb  because in order to answer that question  what matters most to you and why  i really had to sit down and think of  different episodes in my life  that were impactful to me and try to  see if they were coming themes so being  able to do that exercise was extremely  valuable  but then also before i started my first  year out of jsb  i actually spent one week by myself i  went to colorado  um and i spent that entire time trying  to reflect on ways i wanted to approach  my first year of the mba  and i found out to be extremely valuable  when i came here  even though it wasn't a  framework that i stuck to entirely at  least i had  a guiding post i knew what was important  to me so i knew what opportunities to  apply to  i knew what not to pay as much attention  to because the gsb throws so much at you  that if you don't take that time to  reflect you just might  drown a little bit um and it's been  useful to me as well as i kept going  through the year so i've made it a habit  to journal as often as i could  to make sure i'm not wasting my time on  gsb because time flies so fast  so if you don't really take the time to  reflect it's almost like  you're not making the most of the  experience and most recently as i've  been trying to decide  on what to focus on over the summer and  for my second year  of the of the mba program reflection has  given me so much peace of mind because  i've been able to identify things that  really matter to me  um and that's been super gratifying  thank you  yeah i can go ahead um although i'm not  part of the admissions uh committee  i had some conversation with we had